    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Find, to the nearest cent:\n(a) the price of a $\\$78$ grocery basket after $4$ years of $4.2\\%$ annual inflation\n(b) the value of a $\\$1600$ collectible after $5$ years of $6.5\\%$ annual appreciation.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $PV=78$, $r=0.042$, $n=4$.\n$FV=78(1.042)^4\\approx\\$91.95$.\n(b) $PV=1600$, $r=0.065$, $n=5$.\n$FV=1600(1.065)^5\\approx\\$2192.14$. Both calculations use repeated percentage growth."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A pair of shoes costs $\\$210$ now. Assuming annual inflation of $3.5\\%$ over the last $6$ years, estimate its price six years ago, to the nearest cent.",
        "solution_text": "$210=PV(1.035)^6$.\nDivide by the complete growth factor:\n$PV=\\dfrac{210}{(1.035)^6}\\approx\\$170.84$. Multiplying would project forwards instead of undoing the increase."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "An artwork bought for $\\$900$ appreciates at $8\\%$ p.a. for $4$ years. Find its expected value, to the nearest cent.",
        "solution_text": "$FV=900(1.08)^4=\\$1224.440064\\approx\\$1224.44$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Find the final price or value, to the nearest cent.\n(a) A $\\$72$ ticket rises by $2.5\\%$, $4\\%$ and $3\\%$ in three successive years.\n(b) An asset starts at $\\$13\\,500$, appreciates at $6\\%$ p.a. for $3$ years, then at $4.5\\%$ p.a. for $2$ more years.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Apply each rate to the new price:\n$FV=72(1.025)(1.04)(1.03)=\\$79.05456\\approx\\$79.05$.\n(b) Group repeated factors for each rate:\n$FV=13500(1.06)^3(1.045)^2\\approx\\$17\\,558.36$. Do not add or average the rates."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) An item bought for $\\$1800$ was expected to appreciate at $7.5\\%$ p.a. for $5$ years, then sold for $\\$2700$. Find how much the sale price exceeded the expected value.\n(b) Another item bought for $\\$1450$ was expected to appreciate at $6\\%$ p.a. for $4$ years, then sold for $\\$1700$. Was the sale above or below expectation, and by how much? Give differences to the nearest cent.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Expected value $=1800(1.075)^5\\approx\\$2584.13$.\n$\\$2700$ is greater, so excess $=2700-1800(1.075)^5\\approx\\$115.87$.\n(b) Expected value $=1450(1.06)^4\\approx\\$1830.59$.\n$\\$1700$ is smaller, so it sold below expectation by $1450(1.06)^4-1700\\approx\\$130.59$. Keep full calculator values until subtracting."
      }
    ],
